    "CVE-2026-123633"
  ],
  "summary": "When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured to use HTTP/2 for client connections and proxy client requests to a…",
  "details": "When NGINX Plus or NGINX Open Source is configured to use HTTP/2 for client connections and proxy client requests to a backend, a specially crafted request can result in use-after-free in the worker process, if this process is running low on worker_connections. Additionally, attackers can execute code on systems with Address Space Layout Randomization (ASLR) disabled or when the attacker can bypass ASLR.\n\n\n\n\nImpact:\n\n\n\nThis vulnerability may allow remote attackers to cause a denial-of-service (DoS) on the NGINX system or may allow a code execution. There is no control plane exposure; this is a data plane issue only.\n\n\n\nNote: Software versions which have reached End of Technical Support (EoTS) are not evaluated.",
  "severity": [
